SEQUENCE ALIGNMENT
------------------

Input data: 391 taxa with 3 partitions and 9031 total sites (0.0855252% missing data)

  ID	Type	Seq	Site	Unique	Infor	Invar	Const	Name
   1	DNA	389	1510	738	341	909	909	LTRregion_DNA
   2	DNA	391	489	154	59	367	367	env_DNA_CP1
   3	DNA	391	7032	2208	1302	4812	4812	rest_DNA

Column meanings:
  Unique: Number of unique site patterns
  Infor:  Number of parsimony-informative sites
  Invar:  Number of invariant sites
  Const:  Number of constant sites (can be subset of invariant sites)

ModelFinder
-----------

Best-fit model according to BIC: TIM2+F+R3:LTRregion_DNA,HKY+I+R2:env_DNA_CP1,TIM3+F+I+R3:rest_DNA

List of best-fit models per partition:

  ID  Model                  LogL         AIC      w-AIC        AICc     w-AICc         BIC      w-BIC
   1  TIM2+F+R3        -10627.951   21277.902 - 2.73e-312   21278.078 - 5.74e-317   21336.421 -        0
   2  HKY+I+R2          -2272.695    4555.391 - 2.73e-312    4555.515 - 5.74e-317    4576.352 -        0
   3  TIM3+F+I+R3      -38420.797   76865.594 - 2.73e-312   76865.639 - 5.74e-317   76947.893 -        0

AIC, w-AIC   : Akaike information criterion scores and weights.
AICc, w-AICc : Corrected AIC scores and weights.
BIC, w-BIC   : Bayesian information criterion scores and weights.

Plus signs denote the 95% confidence sets.
Minus signs denote significant exclusion.

SUBSTITUTION PROCESS
--------------------

Edge-linked-proportional partition model with separate substitution models and separate rates across sites

  ID  Model           Speed  Parameters
   1  TIM2+F+R3      1.4531  TIM2{2.17966,21.2148,12.7351}+F{0.209788,0.339964,0.238812,0.211436}+R3{0.758103,0.345335,0.221428,2.32883,0.0204682,10.8721}
   2  HKY+F+I+R2     0.6981  HKY{8.05574}+F{0.202434,0.326756,0.214743,0.256067}+I{0.531721}+R2{0.460418,1.70523,0.00786129,27.3341}
   3  TIM3+F+I+R3    0.9237  TIM3{1.07375,19.2687,8.63332}+F{0.237492,0.353786,0.17593,0.232792}+I{0.472591}+R3{0.501624,1.54617,0.0242882,7.39987,0.00149764,29.8317}

